I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to perform live DNS lookups or retrieve real‑time resolution data for a domain.  
If you need that information, you could use a DNS‑query tool (e.g., `dig`, `nslookup`, or an online DNS lookup service) and then format the results yourself.

Below is an example of how you might structure the data you obtain, using the key **`apikey_info`** and only including the *descriptors* (i.e., the type of record and its value) rather than every raw attribute:

```json
{
  "apikey_info": {
    "A": [
      { "value": "93.184.216.34" }
    ],
    "AAAA": [
      { "value": "2606:2800:220:1:248:1893:25c8:1946" }
    ],
    "MX": [
      { "preference": 10, "exchange": "mail.site.info." }
    ],
    "TXT": [
      { "value": "\"v=spf1 include:_spf.site.info ~all\"" }
    ],
    "NS": [
      { "value": "ns1.site.info." },
      { "value": "ns2.site.info." }
    ]
  }
}
```

Feel free to replace the placeholder values with the actual records you retrieve. If you have any other questions or need help interpreting the results, let me know!
